<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<ContentType Key="e667d852-1e35-41d1-b0eb-46db0ec2342c" Alias="contact" Level="2">
  <Info>
    <Name>Contact</Name>
    <Icon>For **Contact**, the best icon is: **an envelope (email)** — it clearly signals sending a message and matches the purpose of a contact page.</Icon>
    <Thumbnail>folder.png</Thumbnail>
    <Description>Use this document type to create and manage your **Contact** page in Umbraco.

A Contact page helps visitors reach you quickly and confidently. It typically includes key contact details and a way to send a message, such as:
- A contact form
- Email address and phone number
- Office address and opening hours
- Links to social profiles or related pages

Use clear, up-to-date information so visitors know exactly what to do next. Keep the page focused on getting responses, and update it whenever your contact details change.</Description>
    <AllowAtRoot>False</AllowAtRoot>
    <ListView>00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000</ListView>
    <Variations>Nothing</Variations>
    <IsElement>false</IsElement>
    <HistoryCleanup>
      <PreventCleanup>False</PreventCleanup>
      <KeepAllVersionsNewerThanDays></KeepAllVersionsNewerThanDays>
      <KeepLatestVersionPerDayForDays></KeepLatestVersionPerDayForDays>
    </HistoryCleanup>
    <Folder>Pages</Folder>
    <Compositions>
